    {
      "title": "try, catch and finally Flow",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "try, catch and finally Flow",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Syntax and Catch Order",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`try` needs ==at least one== `catch` or `finally`",
                "Catch blocks are checked **top to bottom**: ==first matching type wins==",
                "Subclass before superclass, or {red:compile error}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "try { read(); }",
                "catch (FileNotFoundException e) { }",
                "catch (IOException e) { }",
                "finally { cleanup(); }"
              ],
              "note": "subclass first, superclass after"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Multi-catch and finally",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`catch (IOException | SQLException e)` handles ==unrelated== types",
                "`e` is implicitly ==final==",
                "Types cannot be related by **inheritance**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "try",
                    "sub": "risky code",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "catch",
                    "sub": "only if matching",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "finally",
                    "sub": "always runs",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`finally` runs with or without an exception, even after `return`",
                "Skipped only by `System.exit()` or a ==JVM crash=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No return or throw in finally",
              "text": "It ==overrides== the try result and **silently discards** the original exception."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
