                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Suppressed and Java 9",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Body and `close()` both throw: ==body exception is primary==",
                "Close exception attached via `getSuppressed()`",
                "Java 9+: effectively final variable works: `try (res) { ... }`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistake and Interview Point",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Manual `finally { close() }`: verbose, and a failing `close()` can ==hide the original exception=="
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**What is a suppressed exception?** A close() error kept on the primary one",
                "**Close order?** Reverse of declaration, before catch",
                "**Why prefer it over finally?** Shorter, never loses the original error"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
